#, no-wrap
msgid "objecttype"
msgstr "objecttype"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:141
msgid "The type of the object (`blob`, `tree`, `commit`, `tag`)."
msgstr "オブジェクトのタイプ( `blob` 、`tree` 、 `commit` 、`tag` )。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:142
#, no-wrap
msgid "objectsize"
msgstr "objectsize"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:146
msgid ""
"The size of the object (the same as 'git cat-file -s' reports).  Append `:"
"disk` to get the size, in bytes, that the object takes up on disk. See the "
"note about on-disk sizes in the `CAVEATS` section below."
msgstr ""
"オブジェクトのサイズ(`git cat-file -s` がレポートするものと同じです)。 `:"
"disk` を追加して、オブジェクトがディスク上で占めるサイズをバイト単位で取得で"
"きます。以下の「CAVEATS」(注意事項)セクションのディスク上のサイズに関する注記"
"を参照してください。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:146
#, no-wrap
msgid "objectname"
msgstr "objectname"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:152
msgid ""
"The object name (aka SHA-1).  For a non-ambiguous abbreviation of the object "
"name append `:short`.  For an abbreviation of the object name with desired "
"length append `:short=<length>`, where the minimum length is MINIMUM_ABBREV. "
"The length may be exceeded to ensure unique object names."
msgstr ""
"オブジェクト名(別名SHA-1)。オブジェクト名のあいまいでない省略形については、 "
"`:short` を追加してください。目的の長さのオブジェクト名の省略形については、  "
"`:short=<length>` を追加します。ここで、最小の長さは MINIMUM_ABBREV です。一"
"意のオブジェクト名を確保するために、指定の長さを超える場合があります。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:152
#, no-wrap
msgid "deltabase"
msgstr "deltabase"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:156
msgid ""
"This expands to the object name of the delta base for the given object, if "
"it is stored as a delta.  Otherwise it expands to the null object name (all "
"zeroes)."
msgstr ""
"デルタとして保存されている場合、これは指定されたオブジェクトのデルタベースの"
"オブジェクト名に展開されます。それ以外の場合は、ヌルオブジェクト名(すべてゼ"
"ロ)に展開されます。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:157
#, no-wrap
msgid "upstream"
msgstr "upstream"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:167
msgid ""
"The name of a local ref which can be considered ``upstream'' from the "
"displayed ref. Respects `:short`, `:lstrip` and `:rstrip` in the same way as "
"`refname` above.  Additionally respects `:track` to show \"[ahead N, behind "
"M]\" and `:trackshort` to show the terse version: \">\" (ahead), "
"\"<\" (behind), \"<>\" (ahead and behind), or \"=\" (in sync). `:track` also "
"prints \"[gone]\" whenever unknown upstream ref is encountered. Append `:"
"track,nobracket` to show tracking information without brackets (i.e \"ahead "
"N, behind M\")."
msgstr ""
"表示されたrefから「上流」(upstream)と見なすことができるローカル参照の名前。 "
"上記の `refname` と同じように、 `:short` や `:lstrip` や `:rstrip` を尊重しま"
"す。さらに、 `:track` は `[ahead N, behind M]` を表示し、 `:trackshort` は "
"`>` (ahead) または `<` (behind) または \"<>\" (ahead and behind) または "
"\"=\" (in sync) という簡潔なバージョンを表示します。 `:track` は不明なアップ"
"ストリーム参照が検出されるたびに `[gone]` も出力します。 `:track,nobracket` "
"を追加すると角かっこ(`[` と `]` )無しで追跡情報を表示します（つまり、 `ahead "
"N, behind M` )。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:174
msgid ""
"For any remote-tracking branch `%(upstream)`, `%(upstream:remotename)` and "
"`%(upstream:remoteref)` refer to the name of the remote and the name of the "
"tracked remote ref, respectively. In other words, the remote-tracking branch "
"can be updated explicitly and individually by using the refspec `%(upstream:"
"remoteref):%(upstream)` to fetch from `%(upstream:remotename)`."
msgstr ""
"リモート追跡ブランチの `%(upstream)` と `%(upstream:remotename)` と "
"`%(upstream:remoteref)`は、それぞれリモートの名前と追跡されたリモートrefの名"
"前を参照します。つまり、 refspec `%(upstream:remoteref):%(upstream)` を使用し"
"て `%(upstream:remotename)` からフェッチすることにより、リモートト追跡ブラン"
"チを明示的かつ個別に更新できます。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:178
msgid ""
"Has no effect if the ref does not have tracking information associated with "
"it.  All the options apart from `nobracket` are mutually exclusive, but if "
"used together the last option is selected."
msgstr ""
"refに追跡情報が関連付けられていない場合、効果はありません。 `nobracket` 以外"
"のすべてのオプションは相互に排他的ですが、一緒に使用する場合は最後のオプショ"
"ンが選択されます。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:179
#, no-wrap
msgid "push"
msgstr "push"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:185
msgid ""
"The name of a local ref which represents the `@{push}` location for the "
"displayed ref. Respects `:short`, `:lstrip`, `:rstrip`, `:track`, `:"
"trackshort`, `:remotename`, and `:remoteref` options as `upstream` does. "
"Produces an empty string if no `@{push}` ref is configured."
msgstr ""
"表示されたrefの `@{push}` の場所を表すローカルrefの名前。 `upstream` と同様"
"に `:short` ・ `:lstrip` ・ `:rstrip` ・ `:track` ・ `:trackshort` ・ `:"
"remotename` ・ `:remoteref` オプションを尊重します。 `@{push}` refが設定され"
"ていない場合、空の文字列を生成します。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:186
#, no-wrap
msgid "HEAD"
msgstr "HEAD"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:189
msgid ""
"'*' if HEAD matches current ref (the checked out branch), ' ' otherwise."
msgstr ""
"HEADが現在のref (チェックアウトされたブランチ)と一致する場合は `*` 、それ以外"
"の場合は ' ' 。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:190
#, no-wrap
msgid "color"
msgstr "color"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:195
msgid ""
"Change output color. Followed by `:<colorname>`, where color names are "
"described under Values in the \"CONFIGURATION FILE\" section of linkgit:git-"
"config[1].  For example, `%(color:bold red)`."
msgstr ""
"出力色を変更します。 その後に `:<colorname>` が続きます。色の名前は、 "
"linkgit:git-config[1] の「CONFIGURATION FILE」セクションの「Values」で説明さ"
"れています。 たとえば、 `%(color:bold red)` です。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:196
#, no-wrap
msgid "align"
msgstr "align"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:210
msgid ""
"Left-, middle-, or right-align the content between %(align:...) and %(end). "
"The \"align:\" is followed by `width=<width>` and `position=<position>` in "
"any order separated by a comma, where the `<position>` is either left, right "
"or middle, default being left and `<width>` is the total length of the "
"content with alignment. For brevity, the \"width=\" and/or \"position=\" "
"prefixes may be omitted, and bare <width> and <position> used instead.  For "
"instance, `%(align:<width>,<position>)`. If the contents length is more than "
"the width then no alignment is performed. If used with `--quote` everything "
"in between %(align:...) and %(end) is quoted, but if nested then only the "
"topmost level performs quoting."
msgstr ""
"コンテンツを %(align:...) から %(end) の間で左揃え、中央揃え、または右揃えに"
"します。 `align:` の後には、 `width=<width>` と `position=<position>` がコン"
"マ(`,`)で区切られた任意の順序で続きます。ここで、 `<position>` は left また"
"は right または middle のいずれかで、`<position>` の デフォルトは left で "
"`<width>` のデフォルトは配置されたコンテンツの全長です。 簡潔にするために、 "
"`width=` および/または `position=` プレフィックスを省略して、代わりに裸の "
"<width> および <position> を使用することができます。 たとえば、 `%(align:"
"<width>,<position>)` です。 コンテンツの長さがwidthよりも大きい場合、位置合わ"
"せは実行されません。 `--quote` とともに使用すると、 %(align:...) から %(end) "
"の間のすべてがクォートされまれますが、ネストされている場合は、最上位レベルの"
"みがクォートされます。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:211
#, no-wrap
msgid "if"
msgstr "if"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:223
msgid ""
"Used as %(if)...%(then)...%(end) or %(if)...%(then)...%(else)...%(end).  If "
"there is an atom with value or string literal after the %(if) then "
"everything after the %(then) is printed, else if the %(else) atom is used, "
"then everything after %(else) is printed. We ignore space when evaluating "
"the string before %(then), this is useful when we use the %(HEAD) atom which "
"prints either \"*\" or \" \" and we want to apply the 'if' condition only on "
"the 'HEAD' ref.  Append \":equals=<string>\" or \":notequals=<string>\" to "
"compare the value between the %(if:...) and %(then) atoms with the given "
"string."
msgstr ""
"%(if) … %(then) … %(end) または %(if) … %(then) … %(else) … %(end) として使用"
"されます。  %(if) の後に値または文字列リテラルを持つアトムがある場合は、 "
"%(then) の後のすべてが出力されます。そうでない場合、 %(else) アトムが使用され"
"ている場合は、 %(else) の後のすべてが出力されます。 %(then) の前の文字列を評"
"価するときはスペースを無視します。これは、 `*` または ` ` のいずれかを出力す"
"る %(HEAD) アトムを使用し、 HEAD ref にのみ if 条件を適用する場合に役立ちま"
"す。 `:equals=<string>` または `:notequals=<string>` を追加して、 %(if:...) "
"アトムと %(then) アトムの間の値を指定された文字列と比較します。(訳注:つま"
"り、 %(if) から %(then) の間がconditionである)"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:224
#, no-wrap
msgid "symref"
msgstr "symref"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:229
msgid ""
"The ref which the given symbolic ref refers to. If not a symbolic ref, "
"nothing is printed. Respects the `:short`, `:lstrip` and `:rstrip` options "
"in the same way as `refname` above."
msgstr ""
"与えられたシンボリックrefが参照するref。シンボリックrefでない場合、何も出力さ"
"れません。上記の `refname` と同じ方法で、 `:short` と `:lstrip` と `:rstrip` "
"オプションを尊重します。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:230
#, no-wrap
msgid "signature"
msgstr "signature"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:232
msgid "The GPG signature of a commit."
msgstr "コミットのGPG署名。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:233
#, no-wrap
msgid "signature:grade"
msgstr "signature:grade"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:240
msgid ""
"Show \"G\" for a good (valid) signature, \"B\" for a bad signature, \"U\" "
"for a good signature with unknown validity, \"X\" for a good signature that "
"has expired, \"Y\" for a good signature made by an expired key, \"R\" for a "
"good signature made by a revoked key, \"E\" if the signature cannot be "
"checked (e.g. missing key) and \"N\" for no signature."
msgstr ""
"良好(good)な(有効な)署名には「G」、 不良(bad)な署名には「B」、 有効性が不明"
"(unknown)な良好な署名には「U」、有効期限が切れた(eXpired)良好な署名には"
"「X」、 期限切れのキーによって作成された正常な署名には「Y」、 取り消された"
"キーによって作成された正常な署名には「R」、 (キーが見つからないなど)署名を"
"チェックできない場合は「E」、 署名がない場合(no signature)は「N」です。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:241
#, no-wrap
msgid "signature:signer"
msgstr "signature:signer"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:243
msgid "The signer of the GPG signature of a commit."
msgstr "コミットのGPG署名の署名者。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:244
#, no-wrap
msgid "signature:key"
msgstr "signature:key"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:246
msgid "The key of the GPG signature of a commit."
msgstr "コミットのGPG署名のキー。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:247
#, no-wrap
msgid "signature:fingerprint"
msgstr "signature:fingerprint"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:249
msgid "The fingerprint of the GPG signature of a commit."
msgstr "コミットのGPG署名のフィンガープリント。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:250
#, no-wrap
msgid "signature:primarykeyfingerprint"
msgstr "signature:primarykeyfingerprint"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:252
msgid "The primary key fingerprint of the GPG signature of a commit."
msgstr "コミットの GPG 署名の主キー(primary key)のフィンガープリント。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:253
#, no-wrap
msgid "signature:trustlevel"
msgstr "signature:trustlevel"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:256
msgid ""
"The trust level of the GPG signature of a commit. Possible outputs are "
"`ultimate`, `fully`, `marginal`, `never` and `undefined`."
msgstr ""
"コミットの GPG 署名の信頼レベル(trust level)。 可能な出力は、 `ultimate`, "
"`fully`, `marginal`, `never`, `undefined` です。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:257
#, no-wrap
msgid "worktreepath"
msgstr "worktreepath"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:261
msgid ""
"The absolute path to the worktree in which the ref is checked out, if it is "
"checked out in any linked worktree. Empty string otherwise."
msgstr ""
"リンクされたワークツリー(linked worktree)でチェックアウトされている場合、ref"
"がチェックアウトされているワークツリーへの絶対パス。それ以外の場合は空文字列"
"です。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:262
#, no-wrap
msgid "ahead-behind:<committish>"
msgstr "ahead-behind:<committish>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:266
msgid ""
"Two integers, separated by a space, demonstrating the number of commits "
"ahead and behind, respectively, when comparing the output ref to the "
"`<committish>` specified in the format."
msgstr ""
"空白で区切られた2つの整数が、 書式内で指定された `<committish>` と出力refを比"
"較したときの、 それぞれ前方と後方のコミット数をあらわします。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:267
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "ahead-behind:<committish>"
msgid "is-base:<committish>"
msgstr "ahead-behind:<committish>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:274
msgid ""
"In at most one row, `(<committish>)` will appear to indicate the ref that is "
"most likely the ref used as a starting point for the branch that produced "
"`<committish>`. This choice is made using a heuristic: choose the ref that "
"minimizes the number of commits in the first-parent history of "
"`<committish>` and not in the first-parent history of the ref."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:277
msgid ""
"For example, consider the following figure of first-parent histories of "
"several refs:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:289
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*--*--*--*--*--* refs/heads/A\n"
"\\\n"
" \\\n"
"  *--*--*--* refs/heads/B\n"
"   \\     \\\n"
"    \\     \\\n"
"     *     * refs/heads/C\n"
"      \\\n"
"       \\\n"
"\t*--* refs/heads/D\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:293
msgid ""
"Here, if `A`, `B`, and `C` are the filtered references, and the format "
"string is `%(refname):%(is-base:D)`, then the output would be"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:298
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"refs/heads/A:\n"
"refs/heads/B:(D)\n"
"refs/heads/C:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:304
msgid ""
"This is because the first-parent history of `D` has its earliest "
"intersection with the first-parent histories of the filtered refs at a "
"common first-parent ancestor of `B` and `C` and ties are broken by the "
"earliest ref in the sorted order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:308
msgid ""
"Note that this token will not appear if the first-parent history of "
"`<committish>` does not intersect the first-parent histories of the filtered "
"refs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:309
#, no-wrap
msgid "describe[:options]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:313
msgid ""
"A human-readable name, like linkgit:git-describe[1]; empty string for "
"undescribable commits. The `describe` string may be followed by a colon and "
"one or more comma-separated options."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:315
#, no-wrap
msgid "tags=<bool-value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:319
msgid ""
"Instead of only considering annotated tags, consider lightweight tags as "
"well; see the corresponding option in linkgit:git-describe[1] for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:319
#, no-wrap
msgid "abbrev=<number>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:322
msgid ""
"Use at least <number> hexadecimal digits; see the corresponding option in "
"linkgit:git-describe[1] for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:322
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "<pattern>..."
msgid "match=<pattern>"
msgstr "<pattern>..."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:326
msgid ""
"Only consider tags matching the given `glob(7)` pattern, excluding the "
"\"refs/tags/\" prefix; see the corresponding option in linkgit:git-"
"describe[1] for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:326
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "<pattern>..."
msgid "exclude=<pattern>"
msgstr "<pattern>..."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:330
msgid ""
"Do not consider tags matching the given `glob(7)` pattern, excluding the "
"\"refs/tags/\" prefix; see the corresponding option in linkgit:git-"
"describe[1] for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:337
msgid ""
"In addition to the above, for commit and tag objects, the header field names "
"(`tree`, `parent`, `object`, `type`, and `tag`) can be used to specify the "
"value in the header field.  Fields `tree` and `parent` can also be used with "
"modifier `:short` and `:short=<length>` just like `objectname`."
msgstr ""
"上記に加えて、commitとtagオブジェクトの場合、ヘッダーフィールド名(`tree` と "
"`parent` と `object` と `type` と `tag`)を使用して、ヘッダーフィールドの値を"
"指定できます。 フィールド `tree` と `parent` は、 `objectname` と同じように、"
"修飾子 `:short` や `:short=<length>` とともに使用することもできます。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:342
msgid ""
"For commit and tag objects, the special `creatordate` and `creator` fields "
"will correspond to the appropriate date or name-email-date tuple from the "
"`committer` or `tagger` fields depending on the object type.  These are "
"intended for working on a mix of annotated and lightweight tags."
msgstr ""
"commitオブジェクトとtagオブジェクトの場合、特別な `creatordate` フィールドと "
"`creator` フィールドは、オブジェクトタイプに応じて、 `committer` または "
"`tagger` フィールドの適切な日付またはname-email-dateタプルに対応します。これ"
"らは、注釈付きタグと軽量タグの組み合わせでの作業を目的としています。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:346
msgid ""
"For tag objects, a `fieldname` prefixed with an asterisk (`*`) expands to "
"the `fieldname` value of the peeled object, rather than that of the tag "
"object itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:357
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Fields that have name-email-date tuple as its value (`author`, "
#| "`committer`, and `tagger`) can be suffixed with `name`, `email`, and "
#| "`date` to extract the named component.  For email fields (`authoremail`, "
#| "`committeremail` and `taggeremail`), `:trim` can be appended to get the "
#| "email without angle brackets, and `:localpart` to get the part before the "
#| "`@` symbol out of the trimmed email."
msgid ""
"Fields that have name-email-date tuple as its value (`author`, `committer`, "
"and `tagger`) can be suffixed with `name`, `email`, and `date` to extract "
"the named component.  For email fields (`authoremail`, `committeremail` and "
"`taggeremail`), `:trim` can be appended to get the email without angle "
"brackets, and `:localpart` to get the part before the `@` symbol out of the "
"trimmed email. In addition to these, the `:mailmap` option and the "
"corresponding `:mailmap,trim` and `:mailmap,localpart` can be used (order "
"does not matter) to get values of the name and email according to the ."
"mailmap file or according to the file set in the mailmap.file or mailmap."
"blob configuration variable (see linkgit:gitmailmap[5])."
msgstr ""
"name-email-dateタプルを値として持つフィールド(`author` と `committer` と "
"`tagger`)には、名前付きコンポーネントを抽出するために `name` と `email` と "
"`date` の接尾辞を付けることができます。メールフィールド(`authoremail` と "
"`committeremail` と `taggeremail`)の場合、 `:trim` を追加すると山かっこ(`<`, "
"`>`)なしでメールを取得し、 `:localpart` を追加すると電子メールアドレスをトリ"
"ミングして `@` 記号の前の部分を取得できます。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:359
msgid "The raw data in an object is `raw`."
msgstr "オブジェクトの生データは `raw` です。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:360
#, no-wrap
msgid "raw:size"
msgstr "raw:size"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:362
msgid "The raw data size of the object."
msgstr "オブジェクトの生データサイズ。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:366
msgid ""
"Note that `--format=%(raw)` can not be used with `--python`, `--shell`, `--"
"tcl`, because such language may not support arbitrary binary data in their "
"string variable type."
msgstr ""
"注意: `--format=%(raw)` は、 `--python` や `--shell` や `--tcl` と一緒に使用"
"できないことに注意してください。これらのプログラム言語は、文字列変数タイプで"
"任意のバイナリデータをサポートしていない可能性があるためです。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:369
msgid ""
"The message in a commit or a tag object is `contents`, from which `contents:"
"<part>` can be used to extract various parts out of:"
msgstr ""
"コミットまたはタグオブジェクト内のメッセージは `contents` であり、そこから "
"`contents:<part>` を使用して以下によりさまざまな部分を抽出できます:"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:370
#, no-wrap
msgid "contents:size"
msgstr "contents:size"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:372
msgid "The size in bytes of the commit or tag message."
msgstr "コミットメッセージまたはタグメッセージのバイト単位のサイズ。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:373
#, no-wrap
msgid "contents:subject"
msgstr "contents:subject"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:380
msgid ""
"The first paragraph of the message, which typically is a single line, is "
"taken as the \"subject\" of the commit or the tag message.  Instead of "
"`contents:subject`, field `subject` can also be used to obtain same results. "
"`:sanitize` can be appended to `subject` for subject line suitable for "
"filename."
msgstr ""
"メッセージの最初の段落(通常は1行)は、コミットまたはタグメッセージの「件名」"
"(subject)と見なされます。 `contents：subject` の代わりに、フィールド "
"`subject` を使用して同じ結果を取得することもできます。 `subject` に追加でき"
"る `:sanitize` は、件名行をファイル名に適した形にします。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:381
#, no-wrap
msgid "contents:body"
msgstr "contents:body"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:384
msgid ""
"The remainder of the commit or the tag message that follows the \"subject\"."
msgstr "コミットメッセージまたはタグメッセージの「件名」に続く残りの部分。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:385
#, no-wrap
msgid "contents:signature"
msgstr "contents:signature"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:387
msgid "The optional GPG signature of the tag."
msgstr "タグのオプションのGPG署名。"

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:388
#, no-wrap
msgid "contents:lines=N"
msgstr "contents:lines=N"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:390
msgid "The first `N` lines of the message."
msgstr "メッセージの最初の N行。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:395
msgid ""
"Additionally, the trailers as interpreted by linkgit:git-interpret-"
"trailers[1] are obtained as `trailers[:options]` (or by using the historical "
"alias `contents:trailers[:options]`). For valid [:option] values see "
"`trailers` section of linkgit:git-log[1]."
msgstr ""
"加えて、 linkgit:git-interpret-trailers[1] によって解釈されるトレーラーは、 "
"`trailers[:options]` として(または履歴エイリアス `contents:trailers[:"
"options]` を使用して)取得されます。有効な [:option] 値については、 linkgit:"
"git-log[1] の `trailers` セクションを参照してください。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:399
msgid ""
"For sorting purposes, fields with numeric values sort in numeric order "
"(`objectsize`, `authordate`, `committerdate`, `creatordate`, `taggerdate`).  "
"All other fields are used to sort in their byte-value order."
msgstr ""
"並べ替えの目的のため、数値のフィールドは数値順で並べ替えられます"
"(`objectsize` 、`authordate` 、 `committerdate` 、`creatordate` 、 "
"`taggerdate`)。他のすべてのフィールドは、バイト値の順序で並べ替えられます。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:402
msgid ""
"There is also an option to sort by versions, this can be done by using the "
"fieldname `version:refname` or its alias `v:refname`."
msgstr ""
"バージョンで並べ替えるオプションもあります。これは、フィールド名 `version:"
"refname` またはそのエイリアス `v:refname` を使用して行うことができます。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:406
msgid ""
"In any case, a field name that refers to a field inapplicable to the object "
"referred by the ref does not cause an error.  It returns an empty string "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"いずれの場合も、refによって参照されるオブジェクトに適用できないフィールドを参"
"照するフィールド名はエラーを引き起こしません。代わりに空文字列を返します。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:412
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "As a special case for the date-type fields, you may specify a format for "
#| "the date by adding `:` followed by date format name (see the values the "
#| "`--date` option to linkgit:git-rev-list[1] takes)."
msgid ""
"As a special case for the date-type fields, you may specify a format for the "
"date by adding `:` followed by date format name (see the values the `--date` "
"option to linkgit:git-rev-list[1] takes). If this formatting is provided in "
"a `--sort` key, references will be sorted according to the byte-value of the "
"formatted string rather than the numeric value of the underlying timestamp."
msgstr ""
"日付タイプフィールドの特殊なケースとして、 `:` の後に日付フォーマット名を追加"
"して日付のフォーマットを指定できます(linkgit:git-rev-list[1] の `--date` オプ"
"ションのが取る値を参照してください)。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:415
msgid ""
"Some atoms like %(align) and %(if) always require a matching %(end).  We "
"call them \"opening atoms\" and sometimes denote them as %($open)."
msgstr ""
"%(align) や %(if) などの一部のアトムには、常に対応する %(end) が必要です。 "
"%(align) や %(if) などの一部のアトムを「開始アトム」(opening atoms)と呼び、 "
"%($open) と表記することもあります。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:420
msgid ""
"When a scripting language specific quoting is in effect, everything between "
"a top-level opening atom and its matching %(end) is evaluated according to "
"the semantics of the opening atom and only its result from the top-level is "
"quoted."
msgstr ""
"スクリプト言語固有のクォートが有効な場合、トップレベルの開始アトムとそれに対"
"応する %(end) の間のすべてが、トップレベル開始アトムのセマンティクスに従って"
"評価され、そのトップレベルからの結果のみがクォートされます。"

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:423
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXAMPLES"
msgstr "EXAMPLES"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:427
msgid ""
"An example directly producing formatted text.  Show the most recent 3 tagged "
"commits:"
msgstr ""
"フォーマットされたテキストを直接生成する例。 直近の3つのタグ付きコミットを表"
"示します:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:430
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:446
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:460
#, no-wrap
msgid "#!/bin/sh\n"
msgstr "#!/bin/sh\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:436
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"git for-each-ref --count=3 --sort='-*authordate' \\\n"
"--format='From: %(*authorname) %(*authoremail)\n"
"Subject: %(*subject)\n"
"Date: %(*authordate)\n"
"Ref: %(*refname)\n"
msgstr ""
"git for-each-ref --count=3 --sort='-*authordate' \\\n"
"--format='From: %(*authorname) %(*authoremail)\n"
"Subject: %(*subject)\n"
"Date: %(*authordate)\n"
"Ref: %(*refname)\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:439
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"%(*body)\n"
"' 'refs/tags'\n"
msgstr ""
"%(*body)\n"
"' 'refs/tags'\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:444
msgid ""
"A simple example showing the use of shell eval on the output, demonstrating "
"the use of --shell.  List the prefixes of all heads:"
msgstr ""
"出力でのshell evalの使用を示す簡単な例で、`--shell` の使用を示しています。 す"
"べてのheadのプレフィックスを一覧表示します:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:453
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"git for-each-ref --shell --format=\"ref=%(refname)\" refs/heads | \\\n"
"while read entry\n"
"do\n"
"\teval \"$entry\"\n"
"\techo `dirname $ref`\n"
"done\n"
msgstr ""
"git for-each-ref --shell --format=\"ref=%(refname)\" refs/heads | \\\n"
"while read entry\n"
"do\n"
"\teval \"$entry\"\n"
"\techo `dirname $ref`\n"
"done\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:458
msgid ""
"A bit more elaborate report on tags, demonstrating that the format may be an "
"entire script:"
msgstr ""
"タグに関するもう少し手の込んだレポートで、スクリプト全体のフォーマットである"
"可能性があることを示しています:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:465
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"fmt='\n"
"\tr=%(refname)\n"
"\tt=%(*objecttype)\n"
"\tT=${r#refs/tags/}\n"
msgstr ""
"fmt='\n"
"\tr=%(refname)\n"
"\tt=%(*objecttype)\n"
"\tT=${r#refs/tags/}\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:472
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\to=%(*objectname)\n"
"\tn=%(*authorname)\n"
"\te=%(*authoremail)\n"
"\ts=%(*subject)\n"
"\td=%(*authordate)\n"
"\tb=%(*body)\n"
msgstr ""
"\to=%(*objectname)\n"
"\tn=%(*authorname)\n"
"\te=%(*authoremail)\n"
"\ts=%(*subject)\n"
"\td=%(*authordate)\n"
"\tb=%(*body)\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:491
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tkind=Tag\n"
"\tif test \"z$t\" = z\n"
"\tthen\n"
"\t\t# could be a lightweight tag\n"
"\t\tt=%(objecttype)\n"
"\t\tkind=\"Lightweight tag\"\n"
"\t\to=%(objectname)\n"
"\t\tn=%(authorname)\n"
"\t\te=%(authoremail)\n"
"\t\ts=%(subject)\n"
"\t\td=%(authordate)\n"
"\t\tb=%(body)\n"
"\tfi\n"
"\techo \"$kind $T points at a $t object $o\"\n"
"\tif test \"z$t\" = zcommit\n"
"\tthen\n"
"\t\techo \"The commit was authored by $n $e\n"
"at $d, and titled\n"
msgstr ""
"\tkind=Tag\n"
"\tif test \"z$t\" = z\n"
"\tthen\n"
"\t\t# could be a lightweight tag\n"
"\t\tt=%(objecttype)\n"
"\t\tkind=\"Lightweight tag\"\n"
"\t\to=%(objectname)\n"
"\t\tn=%(authorname)\n"
"\t\te=%(authoremail)\n"
"\t\ts=%(subject)\n"
"\t\td=%(authordate)\n"
"\t\tb=%(body)\n"
"\tfi\n"
"\techo \"$kind $T points at a $t object $o\"\n"
"\tif test \"z$t\" = zcommit\n"
"\tthen\n"
"\t\techo \"The commit was authored by $n $e\n"
"at $d, and titled\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:493
#, no-wrap
msgid "    $s\n"
msgstr "    $s\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:500
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Its message reads as:\n"
"\"\n"
"\t\techo \"$b\" | sed -e \"s/^/    /\"\n"
"\t\techo\n"
"\tfi\n"
"'\n"
msgstr ""
"Its message reads as:\n"
"\"\n"
"\t\techo \"$b\" | sed -e \"s/^/    /\"\n"
"\t\techo\n"
"\tfi\n"
"'\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:506
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"eval=`git for-each-ref --shell --format=\"$fmt\" \\\n"
"\t--sort='*objecttype' \\\n"
"\t--sort=-taggerdate \\\n"
"\trefs/tags`\n"
"eval \"$eval\"\n"
msgstr ""
"eval=`git for-each-ref --shell --format=\"$fmt\" \\\n"
"\t--sort='*objecttype' \\\n"
"\t--sort=-taggerdate \\\n"
"\trefs/tags`\n"
"eval \"$eval\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:511
msgid ""
"An example to show the usage of %(if)...%(then)...%(else)...%(end).  This "
"prefixes the current branch with a star."
msgstr ""
"%(if) … %(then) … %(else) … %(end) の使用法を示す例。 これにより、現在のブラ"
"ンチの前にアスタリスクが付けられます。"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:514
#, no-wrap
msgid "git for-each-ref --format=\"%(if)%(HEAD)%(then)* %(else)  %(end)%(refname:short)\" refs/heads/\n"
msgstr "git for-each-ref --format=\"%(if)%(HEAD)%(then)* %(else)  %(end)%(refname:short)\" refs/heads/\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:519
msgid ""
"An example to show the usage of %(if)...%(then)...%(end).  This prints the "
"authorname, if present."
msgstr ""
"%(if) … %(then) … %(end) の使用法を示す例。 存在する場合、これは作者名を出力"
"します。"

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:522
#, no-wrap
msgid "git for-each-ref --format=\"%(refname)%(if)%(authorname)%(then) Authored by: %(authorname)%(end)\"\n"
msgstr "git for-each-ref --format=\"%(refname)%(if)%(authorname)%(then) Authored by: %(authorname)%(end)\"\n"

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:525
#, no-wrap
msgid "CAVEATS"
msgstr "CAVEATS"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:533
msgid ""
"Note that the sizes of objects on disk are reported accurately, but care "
"should be taken in drawing conclusions about which refs or objects are "
"responsible for disk usage. The size of a packed non-delta object may be "
"much larger than the size of objects which delta against it, but the choice "
"of which object is the base and which is the delta is arbitrary and is "
"subject to change during a repack."
msgstr ""
"注意: ディスク上のオブジェクトのサイズは正確に報告されますが、どのrefまたはオ"
"ブジェクトがディスクの使用に関与しているかについて結論を出す際には注意が必要"
"です。パックされた非デルタオブジェクトのサイズは、それに対してデルタするオブ"
"ジェクトのサイズよりもはるかに大きい場合がありますが、ベースとデルタのオブ"
"ジェクトの選択は任意であり、再パック中に変更される可能性があります。"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-for-each-ref.txt:537
msgid ""
"Note also that multiple copies of an object may be present in the object "
"database; in this case, it is undefined which copy's size or delta base will "
"be reported."
msgstr ""
"注意: オブジェクトの複数のコピーがオブジェクトデータベースに存在する可能性が"
"あることにも注意してください。この場合、どのコピーのサイズまたはデルタベース"
"が報告されるかは未定義です。"

